The bug occurs because the code does not properly limit the parsing of channel bits to the number of channels defined in the `chmap` structure. As a result, if a USB audio device reports more bits than there are channels, the code can attempt to write beyond the bounds of the channel map array, leading to potential memory corruption or crashes.

